1
00:00:01,626 --> 00:00:03,712
[MARIELA] <i>Your life is so good!</i>

2
00:00:03,795 --> 00:00:06,047
<i>But my daughter…</i>

3
00:00:06,131 --> 00:00:07,757
<i>She just asked for help.</i>

4
00:00:07,841 --> 00:00:10,301
<i>She made some small mistakes.</i>

5
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:12,929
<i>Don't you have a heart?</i>

6
00:00:13,638 --> 00:00:17,600
<i>You have no empathy!</i>
<i>Not even a little bit.</i>

7
00:00:18,727 --> 00:00:19,853
[BEA] <i>Let me deal with Billy.</i>

8
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:22,230
<i>I'll handle her.</i>

9
00:00:22,313 --> 00:00:23,273
<i>I can do that.</i>

10
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:25,024
<i>Mmm, want more?</i>

11
00:00:25,108 --> 00:00:26,401
- [PETER] <i>Yeah.</i>
- [BEA]<i> Hmm, yes?</i>

12
00:00:26,484 --> 00:00:28,153
<i>- Yes, sure.</i>
<i>- Yes? Okay.</i>

13
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:30,739
<i>- Game.</i>
<i>- I'll take care of it. </i>[CHUCKLES]

14
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:32,323
<i>You're the boss.</i>

15
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:36,828
<i>- Wait for me.</i>
<i>- Mm-hmm.</i>

16
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:37,871
[BEA LAUGHS SHORTLY]

17
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:41,249
<i>Here we go.</i>

18
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:43,126
[PETER SLURRING] Yes, baby.

19
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:44,794
[BEA] <i>Here.</i>

20
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:45,712
[PETER] <i>Here we go.</i>

21
00:00:45,795 --> 00:00:46,796
<i>Bottoms up!</i>

22
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,798
<i>- Mm-hmm.</i>
- [PETER CHUCKLING]

23
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:53,595
<i>Oh.</i>

24
00:00:53,678 --> 00:00:55,889
[BEA] <i>It's good, right?</i>

25
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:57,265
<i>Now…</i>

26
00:00:57,348 --> 00:00:58,224
[PETER] <i>Now…</i>

27
00:00:58,308 --> 00:00:59,184
[CHUCKLES]

28
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:02,187
- [BEA]<i> Are you ready?</i>
- [PETER]<i> Yes, I am.</i>

29
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:03,396
<i>Why are you so beautiful?</i>

30
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,523
[BEA] <i>You're just a lightweight.</i>

31
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:11,696
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

32
00:01:21,247 --> 00:01:22,624
[SHUTTER CLICKING]

33
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:26,085
[SHUTTER CLICKING]

34
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:34,636
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

35
00:01:40,850 --> 00:01:42,018
<i>Robbie.</i>

36
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:43,937
<i>Oh, Val.</i>

37
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:46,105
<i>No hard feelings, okay?</i>

38
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:47,649
<i>Absolutely.</i>

39
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:48,817
<i>No hard feelings, ma'am.</i>

40
00:01:50,026 --> 00:01:50,985
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

41
00:01:51,069 --> 00:01:52,070
[JORDAN] <i>Come on.</i>

42
00:01:52,779 --> 00:01:54,489
<i>Why don't you give him a chance?</i>

43
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:56,866
<i>I can ask you the same thing.</i>

44
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:57,951
<i>What do you mean?</i>

45
00:01:59,953 --> 00:02:01,871
<i>You wrote this, right?</i>

46
00:02:01,955 --> 00:02:03,248
<i>Yeah.</i>

47
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:04,874
<i>- But…</i>
<i>- I knew it.</i>

48
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:06,793
<i>But what's written there is true.</i>

49
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:08,336
<i>Yeah.</i>

50
00:02:09,462 --> 00:02:12,590
<i>But you didn't write this</i>
<i>to express Robbie's feelings for me.</i>

51
00:02:15,009 --> 00:02:18,221
<i>You wrote it to express your feelings</i>

52
00:02:18,304 --> 00:02:20,223
<i>for someone else.</i>

53
00:02:20,306 --> 00:02:25,895
[PRECIOUS] <i>I secretly recorded this too,</i>
<i>so I could show it to you.</i>

54
00:02:25,979 --> 00:02:26,980
<i>Here.</i>

55
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:32,819
<i>Your father said</i>
<i>he'll never leave you guys again.</i>

56
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:36,781
<i>Have you made your decision, Billy?</i>

57
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:40,535
<i>I gave Oliver what he wanted.</i>

58
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:42,453
<i>But that's it.</i>

59
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:45,290
<i>This is going to hurt him.</i>

60
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:48,001
<i>Is it just Oliver who will get hurt?</i>

61
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:49,961
<i>Or you too?</i>

62
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:57,051
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

63
00:03:06,978 --> 00:03:08,146
[WOMAN] <i>What the hell?!</i>

64
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:10,398
<i>The road is so wide!</i>
<i>Stop blocking the way!</i>

65
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:13,443
<i>- I'm just over here on the side!</i>
<i>- Ugh! Don't you have eyes?!</i>

66
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:16,321
- <i>Idiot! Just get out of here!</i>
<i>- You're unbelievable!</i>

67
00:03:19,282 --> 00:03:23,620
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

68
00:03:23,703 --> 00:03:30,209
[MARIELA SCREAMING]

69
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:32,754
- [MARIELA SCREAMING]
- M-Ma?

70
00:03:32,837 --> 00:03:33,713
Ma.

71
00:03:33,796 --> 00:03:35,673
Ma?

72
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:37,550
I'm here, Ma.

73
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:39,802
You're having a bad dream.

74
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:41,137
Wake up.

75
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:46,017
Are you okay?

76
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:49,604
- Hm?
- As long as your father

77
00:03:49,687 --> 00:03:51,439
and his mistress are together

78
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:57,695
with that Billy and her little brother,

79
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:01,741
those bastard children…

80
00:04:04,118 --> 00:04:07,080
I will never be okay.

81
00:04:07,747 --> 00:04:09,290
Never.

82
00:04:09,374 --> 00:04:13,002
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

83
00:04:16,172 --> 00:04:17,507
Drink this first.

84
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:21,469
- [BEA] Here. Go on, Ma.
- [SOFT RUSTLING]

85
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:22,637
Drink it.

86
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:25,765
[SOFT RUSTLING]

87
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:28,434
Ma.

88
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:30,603
[SOFT THUD]

89
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:32,355
I told you, didn't I?

90
00:04:32,438 --> 00:04:35,733
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

91
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:37,443
I'll deal with them.

92
00:04:38,444 --> 00:04:40,071
I'm working on it.

93
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:41,531
Especially with Billy.

94
00:04:41,614 --> 00:04:45,076
Mark my words. Billy is going down.

95
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:46,869
So don't think about it anymore.

96
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:49,706
Don't worry about Billy
or any of them anymore.

97
00:04:49,789 --> 00:04:52,834
I'm working on it. Okay, Ma?

98
00:04:52,917 --> 00:04:54,252
Leave everything to me.

99
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:56,129
You hear me?

100
00:04:58,464 --> 00:04:59,924
Now…

101
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:04,262
You need to get up now, Ma.

102
00:05:04,345 --> 00:05:06,055
Get up because…

103
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:10,727
Look at what I ordered!
We've got so much food!

104
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:13,104
We've got grapes and cupcakes!

105
00:05:13,187 --> 00:05:14,647
And…

106
00:05:15,773 --> 00:05:19,319
You don't really eat salad,
but let's try it because it looks good.

107
00:05:19,402 --> 00:05:22,780
And-- Is that pork chop or steak?

108
00:05:23,364 --> 00:05:25,199
I've got you some chicken too.

109
00:05:25,283 --> 00:05:28,411
And I skipped the coffee this time

110
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:30,788
and ordered red wine instead.

111
00:05:30,872 --> 00:05:32,206
Hmm?

112
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:34,751
Come on and eat, Ma.

113
00:05:36,502 --> 00:05:39,047
[BEA] So, what do you want to eat first?

114
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:40,423
- [SOFT THUD]
- Oh.

115
00:05:41,049 --> 00:05:42,383
Look, Ma.

116
00:05:42,467 --> 00:05:43,301
See?

117
00:05:43,384 --> 00:05:45,136
It's still early, but…

118
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:47,722
Mmm! I got you some red wine.
You like that, right?

119
00:05:48,389 --> 00:05:51,684
Well, what do you want?
Pork chop? Or is this steak?

120
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:53,227
There's chicken too!

121
00:05:53,311 --> 00:06:00,026
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

122
00:06:37,688 --> 00:06:39,982
Billy, please. I need more time with him.

123
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:43,236
It's already more than enough that
you were given the chance

124
00:06:43,319 --> 00:06:45,029
to spend time with Oliver.

125
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,781
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

126
00:06:46,864 --> 00:06:49,700
If we're being honest, I shouldn't have
allowed it in the first place.

127
00:06:49,784 --> 00:06:53,871
If you're afraid that the person who was
after me will bother you,

128
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:55,331
that won't happen.

129
00:06:55,414 --> 00:06:56,707
He's been locked up.

130
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:58,709
He's scammed a lot of people.

131
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:01,587
[BILLY] I know my brother will be hurt

132
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:05,341
when he finds out that I stopped you
from seeing him.

133
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:11,097
But it's better this way
than to drag this out.

134
00:07:14,517 --> 00:07:15,768
I'll give you one week.

135
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:23,401
Please, don't hurt my brother anymore.

136
00:07:23,484 --> 00:07:30,032
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

137
00:07:46,382 --> 00:07:48,509
[MUSIC FADES]

138
00:07:48,593 --> 00:07:49,802
Thank you, thank you, thank you!

139
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:51,095
I super like my room.

140
00:07:51,179 --> 00:07:53,222
It's so huge. Wow!

141
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:55,349
I slept so well. I feel so relaxed.

142
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:56,934
Thank you so much, Peter.

143
00:07:57,018 --> 00:07:58,019
But, you know,

144
00:07:58,102 --> 00:08:00,646
I feel like our rooms
should be next to each other.

145
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:02,023
So, you know…

146
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:06,235
I can keep an eye on you
in case you bring a woman over.

147
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:08,488
I'll tell your wife about it.

148
00:08:09,197 --> 00:08:11,240
I won't bring anyone, okay?

149
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:13,326
Okay, relax.

150
00:08:13,409 --> 00:08:15,870
Inhale, exhale, Peter.

151
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:18,039
Just…

152
00:08:18,873 --> 00:08:20,625
do what I asked, okay?

153
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:25,171
Hack into LoveLine ASAP.

154
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:26,839
- Clear?
- Yes.

155
00:08:26,923 --> 00:08:28,174
I'm working on it.

156
00:08:28,257 --> 00:08:29,926
You better be.

157
00:08:30,009 --> 00:08:32,803
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

158
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:34,680
Because if you don't do it,

159
00:08:35,515 --> 00:08:38,309
your photos will go viral.

160
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:39,727
I'm telling you.

161
00:08:42,104 --> 00:08:44,065
And when they do…

162
00:08:44,148 --> 00:08:48,027
Oh no! You'll lose your license.

163
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:50,196
Then…
[BEA GASPS]

164
00:08:50,279 --> 00:08:52,532
your family will disown you.

165
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:54,659
And your wife?

166
00:08:55,952 --> 00:08:57,286
You'll end up getting a divorce.

167
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:59,705
We don't want that, do we, Peter?

168
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:01,290
Do we?

169
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:05,503
So you'll do what I asked, okay?

170
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:09,465
Can I hear you say, "Okay, Bea"?

171
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:13,511
- Okay, Bea.
- Okay.

172
00:09:13,594 --> 00:09:15,096
All right, go on.

173
00:09:15,179 --> 00:09:18,432
Go to LoveList. Hack it now.

174
00:09:18,516 --> 00:09:19,350
Right now.

175
00:09:21,394 --> 00:09:22,603
Thank you!

176
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:24,855
Take care--Oh!

177
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:26,774
I'll order some food.

178
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:28,234
Thank you!

179
00:09:34,156 --> 00:09:39,912
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

180
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:47,878
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

181
00:09:48,671 --> 00:09:51,257
[BLAIRE] Oh, hi, Sir Fab! What a surprise!

182
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:53,426
- Uh, do you want coffee?
- [UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:09:53,509 --> 00:09:56,596
Tea? Juice? Glutinous rice balls
in coconut milk?

184
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:59,098
Uh, I'd like to take a look at
the LoveLine area.

185
00:09:59,181 --> 00:10:00,016
May I?

186
00:10:00,099 --> 00:10:02,059
Um, it's confidential.

187
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:04,520
But you can take a look at me instead.

188
00:10:04,604 --> 00:10:08,274
But I'm an investor, so… may I?

189
00:10:08,357 --> 00:10:09,400
- May you?
- Yeah.

190
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:11,277
Y-Yes, you may.

191
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,528
Please enter.

192
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:14,363
Feel at home.

193
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:15,698
Yeah, yeah. [CHUCKLES]

194
00:10:15,781 --> 00:10:19,410
You have a lot of hardworking agents here.

195
00:10:20,202 --> 00:10:23,497
He said we're hardworking!
Good work, guys!

196
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:26,542
So, does every agent have
their own login credentials,

197
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:31,213
or do they all share accounts
during their shifts?

198
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:33,633
Uh… um…

199
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:35,635
- They have their own login, sir.
- Right.

200
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:39,722
So, you must be
changing passwords often, then.

201
00:10:39,805 --> 00:10:41,182
- Right?
- Um…

202
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:43,017
- Maybe?
- [CLEARS THROAT]

203
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:48,272
So, I mean, what happens if an agent
forgets their password?

204
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:50,608
How do they reset it?

205
00:10:50,691 --> 00:10:52,401
Uh… reset?

206
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:53,944
- Yeah, how do they reset?
- Reset?

207
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:55,780
Um… They…

208
00:10:55,863 --> 00:10:58,574
They… They click "reset password," sir.

209
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:00,201
Yes, they click "reset password."

210
00:11:00,284 --> 00:11:01,369
Right.

211
00:11:02,536 --> 00:11:08,376
Do you run an intrusion detection program
on your network?

212
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:10,211
In-In-Intrusion?

213
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:12,755
Yeah, intrusion detection program.

214
00:11:12,838 --> 00:11:14,256
Intrusion?

215
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:16,926
I-I don't know if…

216
00:11:17,009 --> 00:11:18,469
Maybe extension.

217
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:19,804
I…

218
00:11:19,887 --> 00:11:22,390
[BLAIRE BREATHING HEAVILY]

219
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:23,599
Are you okay?

220
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:26,394
No, I'm Blaire. I'm not "Okay," sir.

221
00:11:26,477 --> 00:11:30,398
Uh, wait a minute.
Um, I-I'll ask Chief Billy, okay?

222
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:31,399
- Yeah.
- Y-You stay here.

223
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:32,900
You wait. You…

224
00:11:33,484 --> 00:11:35,069
- Stay there.
- Okay, okay. I will.

225
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,406
[BLAIRE MUTTERING] Intrusion? Huh?

226
00:11:38,489 --> 00:11:45,204
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

227
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:52,878
[MUSIC BUILDS]

228
00:11:55,965 --> 00:12:02,972
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

229
00:12:04,181 --> 00:12:06,892
[COMPUTER BEEPING]

230
00:12:11,063 --> 00:12:15,234
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

231
00:12:15,317 --> 00:12:18,612
[COMPUTER BEEPING]

232
00:12:24,243 --> 00:12:26,620
Sorry, chief. Sir Peter's here.

233
00:12:27,246 --> 00:12:29,707
Huh? You didn't tell me
he was coming today.

234
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:31,167
He just suddenly arrived.

235
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:33,210
I thought you were expecting him.

236
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:39,717
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

237
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:44,013
[COMPUTER BEEPING]

238
00:12:44,555 --> 00:12:47,266
Then he started asking me
all sorts of techy questions.

239
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:49,643
Huh? What is he asking?

240
00:12:49,727 --> 00:12:56,650
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

241
00:13:12,082 --> 00:13:18,547
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

242
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:21,634
Hi!

243
00:13:21,717 --> 00:13:23,093
- Peter!
- Hi!

244
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:24,887
Sorry, I wasn't expecting you.

245
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:25,804
Hi. Yeah…

246
00:13:27,264 --> 00:13:29,225
[STUTTERING] I was just looking around.

247
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:32,436
Oh, okay. Do you have
any questions or concerns?

248
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:34,104
I can arrange a meeting right now.

249
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:35,648
No, no. No need for that.

250
00:13:35,731 --> 00:13:37,024
I, uh…

251
00:13:37,107 --> 00:13:38,776
Actually, I was wondering about one thing.

252
00:13:38,859 --> 00:13:40,444
- Okay.
- The data.

253
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:41,904
- Mm-hmm.
- Is it, you know…

254
00:13:42,613 --> 00:13:45,032
automatically encrypted
as the phone calls happen,

255
